-    Repair noisy periodic tiles independently inside diagonal ray partitions cast from a multicolor row.
 
-    Input structure:
-    - Black background with one horizontal multicolor run near the middle and no visible grey rays yet.
-    - The run's pixels are processed left-to-right; diagonal black gaps around it correspond to where occluding grey rays will be drawn.
-    - Every 4-connected region outside those future rays contains a noisy periodic two-color pattern.
 
